   32 /// The bounds of the selection. A selection bounds can be either tracked
   33 /// or untracked. Untracked bounds are unsafe beyond the point the terminal
   34 /// screen may be modified, since they may point to invalid memory. Tracked
   35 /// bounds are always valid and will be updated as the screen changes, but
   36 /// are more expensive to exist.
   37 ///
   38 /// In all cases, start and end can be in any order. There is no guarantee that
   39 /// start is before end or vice versa. If a user selects backwards,
   40 /// start will be after end, and vice versa. Use the struct functions
   41 /// to not have to worry about this.
   42 pub const Bounds = union(enum) {
   43     untracked: struct {
   44         start: Pin,
   45         end: Pin,
   46     },
   47 
   48     tracked: struct {
   49         start: *Pin,
   50         end: *Pin,
   51     },
   52 };
